# Dataset. LLVIP is ~15,000 image pairs and is not ours to redistribute.
# Fetch it from https://bupt-ai-cz.github.io/LLVIP/ and run prepare_llvip.py;
# the manifests under data/ pin exactly which pairs were used.
LLVIP/
data/cache/

# Run products: generated images, checkpoints, trajectories, metrics.
# All reproducible from the commands in the README.
outputs/
trajectories/
report/figures/
report/metrics.*
report/per_image_*.csv
report/code_diff.txt
logs/*_loss.csv

# Tracked on purpose, despite sitting in generated directories:
#   data/*.txt            the split - without it the runs are not reproducible
#   data/split_summary.json
#   schedules/            the alpha_bar arrays and checksums for both runs,
#                         which are the evidence that Run B used the powered
#                         schedule and Run A did not
#   logs/env.json         the machine and library versions results came from
#
# For the report submission, force-add the figures you need:
#   git add -f report/figures/fig1_schedule.png

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
